# base_unittests tests that do not pass on Jam OS yet (tools/cr-test.sh base,
# tools/cr/base-run.py). A "[layer] reason" line, then the full names of the
# tests it explains, one a line (a name may use * as the wildcard). Or one
# line "<pattern> <layer> <reason>". The tests are not run (CR_BASE_ALL=1
# runs them anyway and reports a failure as known), so a `base` PASS means
# every other test passed.
#
# Made 2026-10-16 from CR_BASE_ALL=1 runs of the shards of the suites on
# base_unittests relinked against main's libc (tools/cr/base-run.py: each
# suite a program of its own; tests that crashed alone). The layer is the
# track that owns the fix: posix (libc and its call layer), proc (/proc
# files), fs (a file system under /data: extfs, or the mapping calls),
# launch (starting programs: CB5's launcher patch), jit (executable memory
# by capability), toolchain (the link), musl (musl's own behaviour: the
# same on Linux with musl). A cause marked "?" is a guess from the failing call.
# Findings with their evidence: docs/CR-PLAN.md, "CB2 as built" and "CB2b on ext".
#
# The list is for an ext /data (CB2b, 2026-10-16: the 44 file-system tests that
# only a FAT /data fails are in base_unittests.fat.skip, which base-run.py adds
# when the stick's /data is FAT).
#
# Shrunk 2026-10-17 (CB-RM) from CR_BASE_ALL=1 CR_BASE_LISTED=1 runs of base_unittests
# relinked against main 0fa8eea5 (fork, EFAULT, CBF2a/2b/4, ext limits): what
# passed came off, 596 listed became 259 (docs/CR-PLAN.md, "CB-RM"). The run's
# death tests used gtest's fast style then.
#
# Shrunk again 2026-10-17 (CCS) from CR_BASE_ALL=1 CR_BASE_LISTED=1 runs in base's
# own threadsafe death test style (base-run.py's default again): the clone
# child's calls run on a stack of the layer's own, base_unittests asks for
# `svc exec` (it starts itself and test_child_process, programs on /data), FL3's
# exec, and a forwarded signal that allocates nothing. 38 launching tests and the
# four that set the threadsafe style came off; what is left of the two groups
# went into the groups below by cause (docs/CR-PLAN.md, "CCS").
#
# FileLockingTest (7) came off 2026-10-19 (CR-e's base run, RL's record
# locks per inode in the file service): 177 of 177 FileLockingTest*,
# FilePathWatcher* and ProcessMetrics* OK on ext.
#
# Shrunk 2026-10-20 (DC) from CR_BASE_ALL=1 CR_BASE_LISTED=1 runs of the four programs
# relinked against main with DL2's libc (batches 20065511, 20070336): 17 came off,
# the ones that pass for real now: FileUtilTest.DeleteDeep (directory handles,
# DL1/DL2), the thread id and clone ones (D1, D10: ForkWithFlagsTest.UpdatesPidCache,
# PlatformThreadTidCacheTest*, ProcessUtilTest.LaunchProcess), the registers in a
# handler's ucontext (SGR: LoggingTest.CheckCausesDistinctBreakpoints), the eight
# PartitionAlloc Purge* tests and SamplingHeapProfilerTest.GetSamplesWithResidency
# (exact mincore, D7/MC), PartitionAddressSpaceTest.ZeroSegmentInaccessibleEnd and
# StackTraceDeathTest.StackDumpSignalHandlerIsMallocFree (docs/CR-PLAN.md, "DC").

[launch] a program on /data started through init's /svc/exec (a forked child's execve of base_unittests: spawn, wait, exit) gets the hand-over init writes it (CR2F, CR-REVIEW-POSIX Q1 decided A): its directory is /, not its caller's, and it is AT_SECURE, so the crt drops TMPDIR from its environment. CurrentDirectory's child finds itself in / ("/tmp vs. /"); the signal-file tests' child looks for its file (a name relative to the directory) in / and never finds it, so it runs to the test's timeout (KillSlowChild; GetTerminationStatus*: still running). Q1's option C (the directory given as a channel: DL2 built it) does not reach these: init gives the caller's directory only to a child that is not raised, and base_unittests's own list says `right jit` (patch 0913, CR-e), a power, which makes a child raised whoever calls (user/services/init/exec.c raised(): a power can't be passed on, so init can't know the caller holds it); the log says "base_unittests is raised (AT_SECURE): it starts in /" (docs/CR-PLAN.md, "CCS" and "DC")
ProcessUtilTest.CurrentDirectory
ProcessUtilTest.GetTerminationStatusCrash
ProcessUtilTest.GetTerminationStatusSigKill
ProcessUtilTest.GetTerminationStatusSigTerm
ProcessUtilTest.KillSlowChild

[launch] a forked child's execve of a program on /data is spawn, wait and exit (FORK-PLAN section 2, way (a); FX ends it by exec in place): the pid the test watches is the waiting stub's, so /proc/<pid>/stat is the stub's CPU time (about none), not the busy program's. Its /proc/<pid>/fd is asked of the program since PR (GetChildOpenFdCount passes)
SystemMetricsTest.MeasureChildCpuUsage

[proc] ModuleCacheTest.CheckAgainstProcMaps wants two modules (this one and ld-linux.so) and a static program has one: by design. The other /proc tests pass (CBF4; smaps_rollup CBF6)
ModuleCacheTest.CheckAgainstProcMaps

[posix] dlopen() of a library fails (a static program: musl's stub, logged as `dlopen <library>`)
ElfReaderTestWithCurrentImage.ReadElfBuildId
ImmediateCrashTest.ExpectedOpcodeSequence
NativeLibraryTest.LoadLibrary

[posix] RecvPidWithMaxDescriptors sends the socket over itself 16 times; the kernel's cycle rule refuses a channel end into its own channel (ETOOMANYREFS, CU1), where Linux keeps it in flight (CBF2a: RecvPid and RecvPidDisconnectedSocket pass)
UnixDomainSocketTest.RecvPidWithMaxDescriptors

[posix] mkfifo/mknod answer EPERM (lx_mknodat, meta.c: the layer has no named pipes and fs.idl no mknod; a symbolic link and every other call these tests make work on ext)
FileUtilTest.CopyDirectoryExclFileOverFifo
FileUtilTest.CopyDirectoryWithNonRegularFiles
FileUtilTest.ReadFileToStringWithNamedPipe
FileUtilTest.TestNonBlockingFileReadLinux

[musl] fdopen(-1, "w") returns a FILE (musl does not check the descriptor), and the test expects null: the same on Alpine, a test to leave out on any musl build
FileUtilTest.FileToFILE

[toolchain] PartitionAlloc reserves [64 KiB, 4,097 MiB) (a PROT_NONE zero segment, USER_SPACE_ZERO_SEGMENT_SIZE_MB) by its address as one mapping, and the program's image sits at 0x400000 in the way, so it keeps the 64 KiB it assumes. MH made the hint taken and placement top down (nothing else low), but the programs stay at 0x400000 until they are static PIEs: linked at 1 TiB, headless_shell's calls to BoringSSL's undefined weak functions can't reach 0 (CR-PLAN, "MH"). The Begin and End tests pass (End came off in DC: it reads the last byte of the 64 KiB segment and dies, now that MH's placement leaves nothing mapped low); ZeroSegment itself wants the 4,097 MiB ("size >= 4296015872, actual 65536")
PartitionAddressSpaceTest.ZeroSegment

[posix] DL1 regression (found by DC): FilePathWatcherTest.RecursiveWatch times out at file_path_watcher_unittest.cc:1103, where TouchFile(dir) is expected to make two events for the watched directory (one from the watch on dir itself, one from the watch on its parent, which names it). base::TouchFile opens the directory and calls futimens on that descriptor, which since DL1 is a directory channel: libc sends fs.setattr with the path "" on it, and extfs reports a setattr on a walk with no name (fsops.c ev_walk: a directory for the parent only when the path ended in a name) to the inode's own watches alone, so the parent's IN_ATTRIB with the name never comes (an open file keeps its directory and name, files.c at[]; a directory channel does not). The other 164 FilePathWatcher tests pass (docs/CR-PLAN.md, "DC")
FilePathWatcherTest.RecursiveWatch
